        "listening_news",
        "A New Community Grocery Store",
        "Food access and community",
        2,
        7,
        "A news report announces a community-owned grocery store.",
        "Newsreader: Residents of the Oakridge neighbourhood will soon have better access to fresh food. A community-owned grocery store is opening next month in a former hardware shop on Cedar Avenue. The store was created after more than four hundred local households bought small shares to fund the renovation.\nThe store will sell fruits, vegetables, dairy, and bread, with at least thirty percent of its produce coming from farms within one hundred kilometres. It will also offer a small cafe and a community notice board. Unlike a typical supermarket, member-owners can vote on major decisions and receive a share of any profits.\nThe opening has been delayed twice by supply-chain issues and a shortage of refrigeration equipment, but organizers say the equipment is now installed. The store will open with twelve employees, most of whom live in Oakridge.\nTo make healthy food affordable, the store will offer a ten percent discount to customers with a valid student card or a low-income transit pass. A delivery program for older residents is expected to begin in the spring.",
