        "Three committee members discuss how to spend a small employee wellness budget.",
        "Elena: We have four thousand dollars for an employee wellness program, and we need to recommend one option. I suggest a series of guided lunch walks and free healthy snacks.\nJonah: Snacks are nice, but they are a short-term treat. A wellness app with counselling support might help more people, especially those who work remotely.\nRavi: Both ideas have value, but an app is not used by everyone. I prefer a flexible fitness allowance that lets each employee choose a gym, a yoga class, or an activity of their own.\nElena: A flexible allowance sounds fair, but it is harder to administer and track. The lunch walks need no equipment and give people a shared break.\nJonah: What if we combine a smaller fitness allowance with three lunchtime wellness sessions? That would cover both personal choice and social connection.\nRavi: I can support that if the allowance is equal for everyone and the sessions are open to all shifts, including evening staff.\nElena: Agreed. I will draft a proposal with a two-hundred-dollar annual allowance and three drop-in sessions.\nJonah: I will ask payroll how the allowance would be taxed and whether unused money can carry over.",
