        "Maya: The community centre closes at seven, which is too early for people who work until six and still need to exercise or take a class.\nDaniel: I agree, but staying open later increases staffing, heating, and security costs. We need to know whether enough people would actually use the extra hours.\nLily: I spoke with several neighbours, and many parents want a later family swim on Fridays. Teenagers also asked for a supervised evening program.\nMaya: Then we should propose a two-night trial: stay open until nine on Wednesday and Friday for eight weeks. If attendance is good, we can make it permanent.\nDaniel: That limits the cost and gives us real numbers. I can support the trial if the centre uses the same staff for both evenings.\nLily: I will help promote it through the school newsletter and local shops. We can survey visitors each night to learn which activities they value most.\nMaya: Let's ask the manager to include a quiet study room on Wednesdays and the family swim on Fridays.\nDaniel: Agreed. I will prepare a one-page budget and present it at next week's board meeting.",
