        "Ms. Cho: The library has received a grant, and I think we should buy more current books for reluctant readers. Our shelves have many old titles that students do not choose.\nMr. Bell: Books are essential, but students also need better access to digital research. A set of laptops would let entire classes work on projects at once.\nMs. Ruiz: Both ideas help learning, but the room itself is noisy and crowded. If we add a quiet study area and flexible seating, students will use the library more effectively.\nMs. Cho: The space matters, but without engaging books, students may still not come in. I would prioritize new books and a small reading corner.\nMr. Bell: What if we buy a smaller set of laptops, refresh one shelf of popular books, and add a few movable tables?\nMs. Ruiz: That is a balanced plan. I can support it if the quiet area is kept separate from the computer area.\nMs. Cho: Agreed. I will lead a student book-choice survey so the new titles reflect what they actually want.\nMr. Bell: I will research laptop models and make sure they work with the school's network.",
